R-CM3 R-CM19 R-RV1 R-RV2 R-LD4 R-LD7 R-BL5 R-P6 R-PH10 R-PH13 R-EC10 R-EC11 R-EC17 R-CC7 R-PD9 R-SO7 R-PH8 R-OV1 R-SC1 R-H1 Q7: the command code of `remove` with the fake Fx (slice 008), 6 runs on 5 projects (all in one dir with a `.git`).
The calls of one run fix the order of Remove.run!: args, env, clock, cwd, the project (canonical, list_dirs, read_files), canonical of the project file and the record in projects.json, programs and `roc version`, `read_files` of the member files and the talon.toml candidates (one call), the scan (one `read_files` call for each import level, no call when a level has no new file), the ladder (random, copy_tree, the walk, write_atomic of the candidate header, one round of probes, the build, delete of the copy), the second read (talon.toml first, then the header) and one write_atomic (the same order). The scan runs before the ladder, so a failure of R-RV2 has no ladder call.
Run 1 (r1): `remove json`. The scan has 3 levels: main.roc imports `Helpers` and `Gone` (a file that does not exist: it is skipped, Q7), Helpers.roc imports `Inner/Deep` and `Inner/Mid`, Mid imports `Inner/Leaf`, and Leaf imports `Inner/Deep` again (a file of level 3 that imports a file of level 2: it is not read twice). The aliases `parser` (in Helpers.roc), `jsonx` (in Deep.roc) and `util` (in main.roc) are other aliases than `json`: no hit, and `util` is a package of the header, not a local module. The baseline has 1 error in acme/parser and the candidate has the same one: a note and `check: passed`, the build passes, and the header and talon.toml (the key of `[dependencies]` and of `[overrides]`) are written in one call. The pin stays (the header has one).
Run 2 (r2): `remove parser` where the candidate has a new error in the files of acme/json 2.1.0: exit 10 (R-RV1), the message names the package and `--no-check`, nothing is written, no build. Run 3 (r3, `rm`): a new error in an app file: exit 11. Run 4 (r4): an editor changes the version text in the json entry after the first round of probes (hook after the 5th probes call): exit 17, nothing is written, the editor change stays (R-CC7).
Run 5 (r5): the member is a package (`lib/main.roc`, exposes `Lib`): the scan starts at the module Lib.roc (R-LD7), which imports `json.Json`: exit 11, no probe. Run 6: the same package, `remove parser --json`: 2 probes (the baseline and the check, no build: `probes` is 2 and `build` is null in the envelope), and the header is written.
